            <ArticleTitle>Alcohol pain in Hodgkin's disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>895-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Thirty-five patients with Hodgkin's disease experienced alcohol pain. Nodular sclerosis was the predominant histological grade (77%). Alcohol pain was associated with other factors generally considered to indicate an unfavorable prognosis--systemic symptoms, Stage II disease with multiple site involvement, Stage III or IV disease. Enlargment and a rise in temperature of lymph nodes were both present at or appeared at the site of pain in the majority (86%) of patients with this symptom.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
